 **Formulas:**
-*   The rendering equation is adapted to spherical coordinates. The specific mathematical formulation of the spherical wavefront parametrization is referenced as "Eqn. 11" in the source but not explicitly provided in the text [S1].
-*   Loss function: $L = \sum_{i} || T_{predicted}(\mathbf{x}_i, \mathbf{d}_i) - T_{measured}(\mathbf{x}_i, \mathbf{d}_i) ||^2$, where $T$ is the transient response [G: Standard L2 loss is assumed for regression tasks].
-*   PDF for resampling: $P(\mathbf{x}_i) = \frac{L_i}{\sum_j L_j}$, where $L_i$ is the loss at spot $i$ [S1].
+*   The NLOS process is formulated under spherical coordinates [S1].
+*   The loss function $L$ is calculated between predicted transients $\hat{T}$ and measured transients $T$ at each spot $i$:
+    $$ L = \sum_{i} || \hat{T}_i - T_i ||^2 $$
+    (Note: The exact loss formulation is not explicitly detailed in the sources, but standard L2 loss is implied by "loss function between predicted and measured transients" [S1].)
+*   The PDF for resampling is derived by normalizing the loss $L_i$ at each spot $i$:
+    $$ P(i) = \frac{L_i}{\sum_{j} L_j} $$
